  data: {
    LLM: "Suit Conservation: In the 'Mizerka' (Avoidance) round, your lowest cards (2s, 3s) are your most valuable assets. Don't play them until you are forced to. Lead your highest cards early in suits where you are 'safe' (have low insurance cards) to clear the opponents' low cards.\n\nTalon Management: When choosing your exchange, don't just look for high cards. In a trump contract, look for 'voids' (suits you have zero cards in) so you can trump in early. In Mizerka, exchange your Aces and Kings for anything low.\n\nContract Pacing: Track which contracts your opponents have left. If an opponent has only 'Clubs' and 'Mizerka' left, and you are currently in a Mizerka round, you know they are likely to be desperate to lose tricks. Use their desperation to force them into capturing yours.",
    Player: "Suit Conservation: In the 'Mizerka' (Avoidance) round, your lowest cards (2s, 3s) are your most valuable assets. Don't play them until you are forced to. Lead your highest cards early in suits where you are 'safe' (have low insurance cards) to clear the opponents' low cards.\n\nTalon Management: When choosing your exchange, don't just look for high cards. In a trump contract, look for 'voids' (suits you have zero cards in) so you can trump in early. In Mizerka, exchange your Aces and Kings for anything low.\n\nContract Pacing: Track which contracts your opponents have left. If an opponent has only 'Clubs' and 'Mizerka' left, and you are currently in a Mizerka round, you know they are likely to be desperate to lose tricks. Use their desperation to force them into capturing yours.",
