    basic: "Suit Conservation: In the 'Mizerka' (Avoidance) round, your lowest cards (2s, 3s) are your most valuable assets. Don't play them until you are forced to. Lead your highest cards early in suits where you are 'safe' (have low insurance cards) to clear the opponents' low cards.",
    intermediate: "Talon Management: When choosing your exchange, don't just look for high cards. In a trump contract, look for 'voids' (suits you have zero cards in) so you can trump in early. In Mizerka, exchange your Aces and Kings for anything low.",
